  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GRAISEA-2 Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation of Gender Transformative and Responsible Agribusiness Investment in South East Asia (GRAISEA -2) project in Indonesia will involve the role of Oxfam to convene the whole process, Pt. Alter Trade Indonesia (PT. ATINA) as Private Sector who&apos;s supply chain provides the entire value chain system of targeted commodity (shrimp), and number of strategic partners who we will be partnering with to implement the activity. Total shrimp small -scale producers in Pinrang, South Sulawesi Province that will be involved is 600 households.  Based on their organizational objective, the strategic partners will be divided into two categories, i.e. who will implement value chain related activities which are derived from Result -1 Outcome 1.1., 1.2., and Result -2 Outcome 1.1. Second one is partners who will be involved in the implementation of policy and influencing.  Project also seeks the involvement of relevant parties who can provide services to strengthening meso level particularly the aspects which relates to financial inclusion and sustainable mentorship.  Project will be focusing on valid information to enabling the process to continue. Two research studies will be done participatory, led by external party, the consultant. First is gender market mapping that will describe women position and status along the value chain. It will also provide the information regarding dis/enabling environment for women to participate or take the leadership. An external party, a consultant, will be involved to do the desk research and value chain analysis before bringing the result to be discussed further by the taskforce.   Second is vulnerability risk assessment that will help to develop the wide range stakeholder about the main hazard and issues affecting people in a social -ecological landscape.      Both document development involves taskforce role (representatives of farmer groups champions, PT. ATINA&apos;s Internal Control System (ICS), and government) that will be used to develop anot</narrative>
  </description>
